@@ -0,0 +1,88 @@
+# logredact
+
+Strip personal data out of log files before sharing them.
+
+```
+python -m logredact [--count] [FILE ...]
+```
+
+Each `FILE` is read in the order given, or standard input when no file is
+given (a `FILE` of `-` also means standard input). Every line is written to
+standard output with three kinds of data replaced; everything else on the
+line, including lines with nothing to redact, is passed through byte for
+byte.
+
+| Data | Replacement | Rule |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| E-mail address | `[EMAIL]` | `jane.doe+test@mail.example.com` → `[EMAIL]` |
+| IPv4 address | `[IP]` | four dot-separated octets, each 0-255 |
+| Payment card number | `[CARD]` | 13-19 digits, optionally in groups separated by single spaces or hyphens, passing the Luhn checksum |
+
+```console
+$ printf 'user jane@example.com from 10.0.0.7\n' | python -m logredact
+user [EMAIL] from [IP]
+
+$ printf 'paid with 4111 1111 1111 1111, ref 1234567890123\n' | python -m logredact
+paid with [CARD], ref 1234567890123
+
+$ printf 'a@b.io 1.2.3.4\n' | python -m logredact --count
+[EMAIL] [IP]
+emails=1 ips=1 cards=0          # on standard error
+```
+
+`--count` prints `emails=N ips=N cards=N` to standard error once all output
+has been written.
+
+Requires Python 3.11 or newer and nothing outside the standard library.
+`src/` must be on `PYTHONPATH`:
+
+```console
+$ PYTHONPATH=src python -m logredact app.log > app.redacted.log
+```
+
+## Exit status
+
+* `0` — all input was read and redacted.
+* `2` — a `FILE` could not be read. The name and the reason are reported on
+  standard error. Output already written for earlier files is flushed and
+  kept, the remaining files are not read, and no `--count` summary is
+  printed.
+
+## What is deliberately left alone
+
+* `999.1.1.1`, `256.1.1.1`, `010.0.0.1` — not IPv4 addresses. A longer
+  dotted run such as `1.2.3.4.5` is left whole rather than having a slice of
+  it redacted.
+* `1234567890123` — 13 digits but fails Luhn. A number next to it still
+  gets redacted: `ref 1234567890123 card 4111111111111111` →
+  `ref 1234567890123 card [CARD]`.
+* Digit runs shorter than 13 or longer than 19 digits, and digits glued to
+  letters (`deadbeef4111111111111111`).
+* `user=jane@example.com` keeps its `user=` prefix; only the address goes.
+
+A card number may be written in groups (`4111 1111 1111 1111`,
+`4111-1111-1111-1111`), but a doubled separator ends the number, so
+`4111  1111 1111 1111` is not treated as one card.
+
+## Layout
+
+```
+src/logredact/__init__.py    redact_line(), Counts, luhn_ok()
+src/logredact/redact.py      patterns, Luhn check, card scanner
+src/logredact/cli.py         argument parsing and streaming I/O
+src/logredact/__main__.py    python -m logredact
+tests/test_logredact.py      unit and end-to-end tests
+```
+
+Replacements are applied e-mail, then IPv4, then card: the earlier
+placeholders contain no digits, so a later pass cannot match inside them.
+Lines are processed one at a time, so arbitrarily large files stream without
+being held in memory. Input is decoded as UTF-8 with `surrogateescape`, and
+line endings are preserved as-is, so undecodable bytes and CRLF files
+survive the round trip.
+
+## Tests
+
+```console
+$ python -m unittest discover -s tests
+```
